nge the niche of a YouTube channel after I buy it?</h3>\n<p>You can change the niche, but doing so carries significant risks to the channel\'s algorithmic health. YouTube recommends content based on established audience behavior. A drastic shift will lead to low click-through rates and high unsubscribe numbers, which signals the algorithm to stop recommending your videos. Additionally, YouTube’s 2026 update on generic or repetitive content means that low-effort niche pivots could lead to demonetization. Incremental content shifts are far safer than total rebrands.</p>\n\n<h3>What happens if the seller tries to recover the account after the sale?</h3>\n<p>Our escrow system is specifically designed to neutralize this threat. Funds remain locked in a secure digital vault until the buyer is promoted to Primary Owner and the mandatory security window closes. If a seller attempts a recovery during the handover, our human moderators freeze the transaction immediately. This vigilant oversight ensures the seller only receives payment once the buyer has permanent, unrevokable control of the asset and all recovery backdoors are closed.</p>\n\n<h3>How long does it take to transfer ownership of a YouTube channel?</h3>\n<p>A secure transfer takes exactly seven days to complete. This timeline is a fixed security protocol enforced by YouTube for Brand Accounts. When a new manager is added, they must wait one week before the system allows them to be promoted to \"Primary Owner.\" Any service claiming an instant transfer is likely bypassing security measures, which leaves the buyer vulnerable to the seller reclaiming the account through recovery settings later.</p>\n\n<h3>Does AccsMarkets verify the revenue of the channels listed?</h3>\n<p>Yes, we utilize human moderation and data verification to audit all listings. We require sellers to provide documented proof of AdSense earnings and traffic sources to ensure metrics are authentic and not botted. This process filters out fraudulent