here and cannot be clawed back.\n- **Step 3: Credential Handover.** The seller provides the login credentials or initiates the Brand Account transfer through an encrypted channel. The buyer now has a window to verify the channel metrics.\n- **Step 4: Final Release.** Once the buyer confirms they have full control and the asset matches the description, the funds are released to the seller. The transaction is complete.\n\n### The Role of the Middleman\n\nDirect payments via PayPal or bank transfers are high-risk. PayPal allows for chargebacks months after a deal, leaving sellers without an account or their money. Bank wires are slow and offer zero protection if the seller disappears. Overseeing a **youtube channel buy and sell** deal requires more than just a software platform; it requires human oversight. If a dispute arises during the handover, a neutral expert reviews the evidence to ensure fairness. For sellers, receiving payments in non-reversible crypto like USDT ensures the transaction is final. Once the verification period ends, the money is yours. No reversals. No surprises.\n\n### The 7-Day Transfer Protocol\n\nYouTube has a built-in safety mechanism that many beginners ignore. When you add a new manager to a Brand Account, they cannot become the Primary Owner immediately. There is a mandatory 7-day waiting period. This is where most scams happen in unmonitored trades. A rogue seller might try to kick the buyer out on day six. Escrow solves this vulnerability. The funds remain locked in the digital vault until that 7-day window closes and the buyer is promoted to Primary Owner. If you want to [buy monetized youtube channel](https://accsmarkets.org/blog/buy-monetized-youtube-channel-safely-the-2026-investor-guide-3330048) assets, this waiting period is your greatest security feature. It gives you the necessary time to verify every metric without the risk of losing your capital.\n\n## <a name=\"critical-red-flags-and-how-to-avoid-account-recovery-scams\"></a>C